02:15:06.021 --> 02:15:06.854
- Okay.

02:15:06.854 --> 02:15:07.687
- Why is "Psyren?"

02:15:07.687 --> 02:15:08.520
- What is "Psyren?"

02:15:08.520 --> 02:15:09.353
What the fuck is that?

02:15:09.353 --> 02:15:10.186
- Shonen Jump.

02:15:10.186 --> 02:15:11.019
- It's Shonen Jump.

02:15:11.019 --> 02:15:12.144
I'm surprised you've heard of "Psyren."

02:15:12.144 --> 02:15:13.594
- I fucking love "Psyren."

02:15:13.594 --> 02:15:14.452
- You love "Psyren."

02:15:14.452 --> 02:15:15.679
Oh my fucking God, yes!

02:15:15.679 --> 02:15:19.963
- That's why I was like,
"Why is this here?"

02:15:19.963 --> 02:15:20.913
- What is "Psyren?"

02:15:20.913 --> 02:15:22.532
- It's one of those,
like, it's one of those-

02:15:22.532 --> 02:15:23.365
- Please explain the plot.

02:15:23.365 --> 02:15:25.215
- Underground Shonen Jump manga that like-

02:15:25.215 --> 02:15:26.048
- Okay.

02:15:26.048 --> 02:15:28.675
- It didn't have very
long run time, did it?

02:15:28.675 --> 02:15:29.834
- I mean, it had like a
good hundred chapters.

02:15:29.834 --> 02:15:30.695
- Did it?

02:15:30.695 --> 02:15:31.528
- It got canceled.

02:15:31.528 --> 02:15:32.361
It got canceled.

02:15:32.361 --> 02:15:33.194
- That's right.

02:15:33.194 --> 02:15:34.027
Yeah it did get canceled.

02:15:34.027 --> 02:15:34.860
- [Connor] All right so, tell the plot.

02:15:34.860 --> 02:15:35.718
- I will tell you the plot.

02:15:35.718 --> 02:15:38.474
Okay, so there's going to
be like a slight spoiler,

02:15:38.474 --> 02:15:40.239
but I feel like it's within
the first four chapters.

02:15:40.239 --> 02:15:41.972
And I feel like it's a big twist

02:15:41.972 --> 02:15:46.722
that I feel is what got me
hooked into this manga, right.

02:15:48.647 --> 02:15:50.242
So, that's the main...

02:15:50.242 --> 02:15:52.108
I can't actually remember
the character names.

02:15:52.108 --> 02:15:53.225
'Cause it's been so
long since I've read it.

02:15:53.225 --> 02:15:54.307
- Yeah, yeah.

02:15:54.307 --> 02:15:57.307
But it's this main character and he,

02:15:58.398 --> 02:15:59.231
I don't think there's
anything too special about him

02:15:59.231 --> 02:16:00.064
at the beginning.

02:16:00.064 --> 02:16:03.694
He runs a service where
he solves problems, right.

02:16:03.694 --> 02:16:05.626
That's got nothing to do
with what happens, right.

02:16:05.626 --> 02:16:09.968
And so he sees this girl, it looks like

02:16:09.968 --> 02:16:12.547
she looks like she's going
through some issues or something.

02:16:12.547 --> 02:16:14.252
So she, he tries to help her.

02:16:14.252 --> 02:16:16.378
And in that process,

02:16:16.378 --> 02:16:20.703
he follows her and then he
gets transported with her

02:16:20.703 --> 02:16:22.460
to just this new place.

02:16:22.460 --> 02:16:25.886
He doesn't know where he is, right.

02:16:25.886 --> 02:16:26.817
- He gets Isakai'd.

02:16:26.817 --> 02:16:28.988
- Yeah, he basically gets Isakai'd, right.

02:16:28.988 --> 02:16:30.057
- So goes to another world.

02:16:30.057 --> 02:16:31.457
- Yeah, yeah, kind of.

02:16:31.457 --> 02:16:32.582
He goes to another world.

02:16:32.582 --> 02:16:35.066
- Ooh I see a theme here Garnt.

02:16:35.066 --> 02:16:35.916
- Yeah, no.

02:16:35.916 --> 02:16:39.486
He goes to another world
with this girl, right.

02:16:39.486 --> 02:16:40.823
And then they're in, just in,

02:16:40.823 --> 02:16:43.327
there's just in this
like barren wasteland.

02:16:43.327 --> 02:16:45.504
And then they get transported
with a bunch of people.

02:16:45.504 --> 02:16:47.373
And it's kinda like the
"Gantz" kind of theme

02:16:47.373 --> 02:16:49.782
where it's not as brutal.

02:16:49.782 --> 02:16:51.523
'Cause it's like Shonen Jump "Gantz."

02:16:51.523 --> 02:16:53.036
So it's not got like massive gore,

02:16:53.036 --> 02:16:55.001
but like people just start
dying left, right, and center.

02:16:55.001 --> 02:16:55.834
- [Connor] Okay.
- Right.

02:16:55.834 --> 02:16:59.784
And for some reason she has
like a special psychic power

02:16:59.784 --> 02:17:01.438
that she uses to survive.

02:17:01.438 --> 02:17:03.447
So he kind of follows her right.

02:17:03.447 --> 02:17:07.179
And so in like fighting through
this kind of "death game",

02:17:07.179 --> 02:17:09.524
kind of barren wasteland kind of thing,

02:17:09.524 --> 02:17:12.009
he like tries to figure
out where the fuck he is,

02:17:12.009 --> 02:17:15.156
how he got there and what
the fuck's going on, right.

02:17:15.156 --> 02:17:17.983
And then it's like the big
twist at the end of episode four

02:17:17.983 --> 02:17:22.558
is that he goes on top
of this like a building

02:17:22.558 --> 02:17:24.870
that's just been like, laying,

02:17:24.870 --> 02:17:28.379
it's like a, what's the
word I'm looking for?

02:17:28.379 --> 02:17:29.308
- Like abandoned or-

02:17:29.308 --> 02:17:31.508
- No, not abandoned, but
it's just like, it's,

02:17:31.508 --> 02:17:32.697
what's the word where it's just like,

02:17:32.697 --> 02:17:35.060
it's been years since
this building's been-

02:17:35.060 --> 02:17:36.437
- Overgrown?

02:17:36.437 --> 02:17:37.270
- Dilapidated?

02:17:37.270 --> 02:17:38.103
- Dilapidated, yeah.

02:17:38.103 --> 02:17:38.936
It's this dilapidated building right.

02:17:38.936 --> 02:17:40.469
And he, and he goes on it

02:17:40.469 --> 02:17:43.202
and then he sees Mount Fuji, right.

02:17:43.202 --> 02:17:45.435
And it's just, he realizes

02:17:45.435 --> 02:17:48.410
that for some reason, he's in Japan.

02:17:48.410 --> 02:17:50.876
He's in a city that is in complete ruins

02:17:50.876 --> 02:17:53.344
and the apocalypse has happened.

02:17:53.344 --> 02:17:56.616
And so he doesn't know how
he got there or where he is.

02:17:56.616 --> 02:17:57.778
- That's right.

02:17:57.778 --> 02:17:59.953
- Or, should I say it?

02:17:59.953 --> 02:18:01.997
Okay, I'm going to say it, okay-

02:18:01.997 --> 02:18:02.830
- Spoiler alert.

02:18:02.830 --> 02:18:04.901
- Or when he is, but-

02:18:04.901 --> 02:18:07.043
- I mean, I guessed when you
had said that he was in Japan

02:18:07.043 --> 02:18:08.419
that is was a time thing.

02:18:08.419 --> 02:18:09.399
- When he said it was dilapidated.

02:18:09.399 --> 02:18:10.857
- Yeah, I was like okay well

02:18:10.857 --> 02:18:13.379
that's a signal the passage of time.

02:18:13.379 --> 02:18:14.212
- Yeah, yeah.

02:18:14.212 --> 02:18:16.759
So, I guess that spoils it.

02:18:16.759 --> 02:18:20.108
But yeah, I mean, so
what I love about this

02:18:20.108 --> 02:18:23.733
is that it's a Shonen Jump action manga

02:18:23.733 --> 02:18:25.491
that has a mystery core.

02:18:25.491 --> 02:18:30.408
Because the core of this is
him going back to his own world

02:18:31.441 --> 02:18:34.298
or his own time and kind of figuring out

02:18:34.298 --> 02:18:35.131
what the fuck happened.

02:18:35.131 --> 02:18:36.326
How did it happen?

02:18:36.326 --> 02:18:39.267
And in that process, like,

02:18:39.267 --> 02:18:40.966
that's all I'm going to say,
because in that process,

02:18:40.966 --> 02:18:43.491
there's so many twists and
turns that come from that

02:18:43.491 --> 02:18:46.197
and him trying to figure
out what's going on.

02:18:46.197 --> 02:18:49.197
And it was just nice to
see like a Shonen Jump

02:18:49.197 --> 02:18:51.059
that has action in it,

02:18:51.059 --> 02:18:53.175
but also has this really mystery aspect

02:18:53.175 --> 02:18:54.800
that keeps you coming back

02:18:54.800 --> 02:18:56.599
and just keeps you like
reading the next page

02:18:56.599 --> 02:18:57.805
just to figure out what happens.

02:18:57.805 --> 02:18:59.438
Because I feel like
there's been Shonen Jump

02:18:59.438 --> 02:19:01.754
with a mystery aspect, for example,

02:19:01.754 --> 02:19:05.522
what's the one where they eat kids, again?

02:19:05.522 --> 02:19:06.355
- "Promise Neverland."

02:19:06.355 --> 02:19:07.188
- "Promise Neverland."

02:19:07.188 --> 02:19:08.021
It's a bit like "Promise Neverland"

02:19:08.021 --> 02:19:08.854
and it's a bit like, obviously-

02:19:08.854 --> 02:19:09.687
- I've never heard "Promise Neverland"

02:19:09.687 --> 02:19:12.212
be described as "what's the
one where they eat kids?"

02:19:12.212 --> 02:19:14.035
- I mean, am I wrong?

02:19:14.035 --> 02:19:15.476
- I don't know why I got it right away.

02:19:15.476 --> 02:19:17.156
- Am I wrong, am I wrong?

02:19:17.156 --> 02:19:18.797
- I mean-
- That is what happens.

02:19:18.797 --> 02:19:21.368
- That is what it is, that is what it is.

02:19:21.368 --> 02:19:23.789
- It's not the one about
the kids trying to escape.

02:19:23.789 --> 02:19:26.848
It is the one where the kids get eaten.

02:19:26.848 --> 02:19:27.881
- Don't fuck around.

02:19:27.881 --> 02:19:30.747
- Like I liked the fact
that it had a mystery aspect

02:19:30.747 --> 02:19:32.949
and also a battle Shonen aspect.

02:19:32.949 --> 02:19:35.090
And I feel like it was so underground.

02:19:35.090 --> 02:19:36.281
'Cause nobody fucking read it.

02:19:36.281 --> 02:19:37.114
- I think the problem with "Psyren"

02:19:37.114 --> 02:19:40.388
is that it kind of came out
at a time where Shonen Jump

02:19:40.388 --> 02:19:42.765
was just absolutely stacked.

02:19:42.765 --> 02:19:44.280
Where like everything else in Shonen-

02:19:44.280 --> 02:19:47.938
'Cause this was like mid
2000's Shonen Jump, right?

02:19:47.938 --> 02:19:50.236
So this was not only in
the midst of the Big Three,

02:19:50.236 --> 02:19:53.044
but also like the lesser
known Shonen Jump stuff

02:19:53.044 --> 02:19:56.604
that was not the Big Three
was still very, very popular.

02:19:56.604 --> 02:19:57.950
- So why did they get canceled?

02:19:57.950 --> 02:20:00.247
- Just because it wasn't popular enough.

02:20:00.247 --> 02:20:01.080
- It just got axed.

02:20:01.080 --> 02:20:02.467
- I'm just like,

02:20:02.467 --> 02:20:03.850
I feel like another thing
